node.doctext:
Obligatory Zalgo-summoning solution:

<code>
#!/usr/bin/perl -p0
s/<!([^<>]|<(?1)*>)*>//gs;
s/<(?!div\b[^>]*\bclass\s*=\s*(['"])data\1)([^<>]|<(?2)*>)*>//gs;
s/.*?<(?:[^'"]|(['"]).*?\1)*?\bid\s*=\s*(['"])(.*?)\2.*?>([^<]*)/$3=$4, /gs;
s/&#(\w+);/chr $1/ge;
s/[^\w=, ]|, $|(.)\1\1//g;
</code>

To make it harder on regexes, I suggest:<ul>

<li>throwing unbalanced <code>[<>'"]</code> inside CDATA sections / comments / attributes (especially <code>class='data"'</code>)
<li>using names that can be confused with the interesting ones: <code><divx</code>, <code>aclass="data"</code>, …
<li>using XML namespaces liberally
<li>using external entities
</ul>
